{"content":[{"c":["ARPHAXAD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Shem’s son and Noah’s grandson, born two years after the Flood. Arphaxad’s descendants were probably the Chaldeans (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.22-24","r":"Gen.10.22-24","rawR":"Gen.10.22-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.22-24","value":"Gen.10.22-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:22-24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.10-13","r":"Gen.11.10-13","rawR":"Gen.11.10-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.10-13","value":"Gen.11.10-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:10-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.17-18,24","r":"1Chr.1.17-18,24","rawR":"1Chr.1.17-18,24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.17-18,24","value":"1Chr.1.17-18,24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:17-18, 24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.36","r":"Luke.3.36","rawR":"Luke.3.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.36","value":"Luke.3.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:36"},"). Arphaxad was born two years after the Flood when his father was one hundred years old (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.10","r":"Gen.11.10","rawR":"Gen.11.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.10","value":"Gen.11.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:10"},") and was the grandfather of Eber, whom some believe was ancestor of the Hebrews (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.17-25","r":"1Chr.1.17-25","rawR":"1Chr.1.17-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.17-25","value":"1Chr.1.17-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:17-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.35-36","r":"Luke.3.35-36","rawR":"Luke.3.35-36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.35-36","value":"Luke.3.35-36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:35-36"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Arphaxad","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:22-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.22-24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.22-24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.22-24"},{"anchorText":"11:10-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?